B.aDs=s(["Atmosphere","Hydrosphere","Biosphere","Geosphere"],t.s)
B.aNQ=s(["Air carries gases and water vapor; clouds contain droplets and/or ice crystals.","Water occurs at the surface, below ground, in organisms, as ice and in the air.","Plants take up water, exchange gases and transfer water to the air by transpiration.","Rock and soil influence infiltration and runoff, while roots help stabilize soil."],t.s)
B.bsf=new A.an("One landscape contains interacting Earth systems","comparison",B.aDs,B.aNQ,"Water arrows show material transfers, with branches and stores. Separate Sun input and outgoing-radiation arrows show energy transfer; energy does not cycle back to the Sun. Simplified sizes, routes and timescales.",B.u,"","g7-earth")
B.aCm=s(["Air to plants","Plants to consumers","Living things to air","Dead material and soil"],t.s)
B.aRg=s(["Photosynthesis incorporates carbon from atmospheric carbon dioxide into sugars.","Feeding transfers carbon in food into consumer bodies.","Respiration in plants, animals and other organisms returns carbon dioxide.","Decomposition transfers carbon through decomposers and can release carbon dioxide; some carbon remains stored in soil."],t.s)
B.bpG=new A.an("Carbon moves among several stores and pathways","comparison",B.aCm,B.aRg,"Selected branches of a carbon cycle, not a compulsory four-step route. Oceans and rocks provide other stores. Carbon matter cycles; captured light energy eventually spreads as heat.",B.u,"","")
B.arl=s(["Rain input","Runoff output","Vapor output","Storage increase"],t.s)
B.aLS=s(["100 L enters the defined plot.","30 L leaves as runoff.","50 L leaves through evaporation plus transpiration.","100 \u2212 30 \u2212 50 = 20 L is the increase in water stored."],t.s)
B.anY=s([100,30,50,20],t.n)
B.brG=new A.an("A simplified garden water budget for one period","bars",B.arl,B.aLS,"Only the stated inputs and outputs apply to this example. Starting storage of 40 L becomes 60 L. Storage increase is not another outflow, and infiltration within the plot is not automatically water leaving it.",B.anY,"L","")
B.aG6=s(["0\u20132 s","2\u20134 s","4\u20136 s"],t.s)
B.aO0=s(["Distance rises from 0 to 4 m: interval speed 4 \xf7 2 = 2 m/s.","Distance remains at 4 m: no additional travel, so interval speed is 0 m/s.","Distance rises from 4 to 8 m: interval speed (8 \u2212 4) \xf7 (6 \u2212 4) = 2 m/s."],t.s)
B.brL=new A.an("Cumulative distance tells a journey\u2019s story","comparison",B.aG6,B.aO0,"Time is horizontal and cumulative distance is vertical. Straight segments represent constant interval speed; corners idealize changes. This graph does not show direction or the forces causing the motion.",B.u,"","g7-motion")
B.aAG=s(["8 N right, 3 N left","5 N right, 5 N left","Weight down, support up"],t.s)
B.aR9=s(["Opposite horizontal forces give a 5 N resultant to the right.","The horizontal resultant is zero; velocity does not change if all other forces also balance.","For a resting object on a level surface, equal opposing vertical forces can balance without either being absent."],t.s)
B.bpS=new A.an("Combine forces on one object, keeping direction","comparison",B.aAG,B.aR9,"Every pair here acts on the same object. Forces on different interacting objects are not added as if they act on one object.",B.u,"","")
B.azd=s(["Journey A: 12 m in 6 s","Journey B: 12 m in 4 s"],t.s)
